# fizzpure.lic
=begin
      author: Fizzlestiks (fork of puritan.lic 1.2.0 by Ondreian)
        name: fizzpure
        game: gemstone
        tags: bard, 1004, purify, purification song, gems, orb gem, pure gem
    requires: Lich > 5.14.2
     version: 1.0.0
        note: Written with assistance from Claude (Anthropic).

  Purifies your gems with Purification Song (1004), one gem at a time, and stops
  singing to a gem as soon as it gets risky. Orb (pure) gems go to their own container.

  Usage:
    ;fizzpure --raw=cloak --orbs=linen.pouch
    ;fizzpure --raw=cloak,backpack,haversack --orbs=linen.pouch
    ;fizzpure --raw=cloak --orbs=pouch --dry-run     list what it would sing to, no singing

  Options:
    --raw=<containers>     where the gems are (comma list; adjective.noun like the game)
    --orbs=<container>     where orb gems go (required, keep it out of what eloot sells)
    --sung=<container>     where purified gems go (default: back where each came from)
    --filter=<words>       only gems whose name has one of these (comma list)
    --max-rounds=<n>       most songs per gem (default 20)
    --min-value=<silver>   skip gems that appraise under this (needs 25+ trading)
    --min-health=<hp>      don't sing below this many hit points (default 70)
    --mana-wait=<seconds>  how long to wait for mana before giving up (default 600)
    --dry-run              list the gems and stop
    --silent               no per-gem report

  When it stops singing to a gem (gswiki, Purification Song (1004), 2026-11-12):
    keeps singing  "...becomes more perfect." / "the gem hums in response to the resonance
                   of your voice" (getting close to what your ranks can do)
    STOPS          "...the crystalline structure of the gem improves somewhat."
                   That's the last fairly safe message; the next ones are "crack loudly and
                   strain" and "severely affecting", and then the gem explodes in your hand.
    STOPS          "cannot be purified any further" (as good as it gets)
    ORB            "...the very essence flows into it filling the imperfections." (just
                   turned into an orb) or "As the gem resonates in response to your voice,
                   you sense that it cannot be purified any further." (already an orb)
  Tiny pearls are always orbs (gswiki "Pure gem"; orb_check found one 2026-10-20), so they
  go straight to the orb container without a song. Mother-of-pearl is skipped (puritan:
  always misfires). Gems on eloot's sell_exclude list are left alone.

  Every song is gated: at least the spell's mana cost in hand right before the SING (no
  overexertion), at least --min-health hit points (an exploding gem can do about 60),
  no wounds worse than minor and not stunned. If a gem explodes, eherbs runs before the
  next one. Anything it can't sort out (no mana after --mana-wait, can't heal) ends the
  run with the rest of the gems left as they are, so a prerest can carry on and sell them.

  Changes from puritan.lic 1.2.0:
    - Stops at "improves somewhat" and at "severely affecting" (puritan kept singing).
    - Tells an orb ("resonates ... cannot be purified") from a maxed gem ("vibrates ...")
      by the song text, so no loresinging; --loresing and --mage are gone.
    - Purified gems go back to the container they came from unless --sung is given, and
      --raw takes several containers.
    - Never takes armor off (puritan did by default), never waits forever for healing or
      mana, and never raises an error mid-run: it puts the gem back and stops.
    - Tiny pearls go to the orb container instead of being skipped.
    - Gems already finished this session are remembered by ID and not sung again.
    - --regain-mana, --herbs, --skip-armor and the hunting.rb team requests are gone.
=end

require 'yaml'

module FizzPure
  VERSION = '1.0.0'
  SPELL   = 1004
  NAME    = 'Purification Song'

  # ---- song outcomes. None of these have been seen in our own logs yet (no 1004 casts
  # as of 2026-11-12): ESSENCE and SOMEWHAT are quoted by Scott, the rest are gswiki's.
  # (the empty right hand afterwards is the real test, see sing)
  SHATTER  = /Your focused voice causes .+ to shatter/
  ESSENCE  = /very essence flows into it filling the imperfections/
  ORB_MAX  = /resonates in response to your voice, you sense that it cannot be purified/
  MAX      = /cannot be purified any further/
  SEVERE   = /resonance of your voice is severely affecting/
  STRAIN   = /crack loudly and strain/
  SOMEWHAT = /crystalline structure of the gem improves somewhat/
  BETTER   = /becomes more perfect|hums in response to the resonance of your voice|smoother and more pure in color|sparkles a little more/
  MISFIRE  = /song misfires|misfires/
  HINDERED = /^\[Spell Hindrance for /
  NOT_HELD = /must be holding|^What were you referring to|^I could not find|^Sing at what|^You are not holding/
  NO_MANA  = /^But you don't have any mana|don't have enough mana|^You don't have a spell prepared|spellsong is not ready/
  SING_RT  = /Sing Roundtime|Cast Roundtime|^Roundtime/
  # any line that says the song was answered, so a short quiet spell after it ends the read
  ANSWERED = Regexp.union(SHATTER, ESSENCE, MAX, SEVERE, STRAIN, SOMEWHAT, BETTER, MISFIRE, HINDERED)
  SING_DONE = Regexp.union(SING_RT, NOT_HELD, NO_MANA)

  PREP_DONE = /^Your spell(?:song)? is ready\.|^You already have a spell readied|^You can't think clearly enough|^You are concentrating too intently|^You are too injured|^But you don't have any mana|^You can't make that dextrous|^You do not know that spell|cough up some blood/
  GET_DONE  = /^You (?:remove|get|grab|pull|take|pick up|carefully remove|retrieve)|^Get what\?|^I could not find|^What were you referring to|^You need a free hand|^You can't/
  PUT_DONE  = /^You (?:put|place|slip|tuck|add|drop|carefully place|gently place)|^I could not find|^What were you referring to|won't fit|^That is closed|too (?:full|heavy|large)/
  APPRAISE  = /worth (?:approximately |about )?(?<value>[\d,]+) silvers?/

  TINY_PEARL = /\btiny .*pearl\b/
  SKIP_NAMES = /mother-of-pearl/

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- options
  def self.opts
    @opts ||= Script.current.vars[1..-1].to_a.each_with_object({}) { |arg, h|
      if arg =~ /\A--([\w-]+)(?:=(.*))?\z/m
        h[Regexp.last_match(1).tr('-', '_').to_sym] = Regexp.last_match(2).nil? ? true : Regexp.last_match(2)
      else
        h[arg.downcase.to_sym] = true
      end
    }
  end

  def self.list_opt(key)
    opts[key].to_s.split(',').map(&:strip).reject(&:empty?)
  end

  def self.int_opt(key, default)
    opts[key].to_s =~ /\A\d+\z/ ? opts[key].to_i : default
  end

  def self.msg(text)
    respond "[fizzpure] #{text}"
  end

  def self.bold(text)
    _respond "<pushBold/>[fizzpure] #{text}<popBold/>"
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- containers
  # "linen.pouch", "linen pouch", "my pouch", "pouch": the last word is the noun and every
  # other word starts a word of the name (same as orb_check / charge_me_up_scotty)
  def self.matches?(obj, name)
    words = name.to_s.strip.sub(/\Amy\s+/i, '').split(/[\s.]+/)
    return false if words.empty?

    obj.noun.to_s.casecmp?(words.last) && words[0..-2].all? { |word| obj.name.to_s =~ /\b#{Regexp.escape(word)}/i }
  end

  def self.find_container(name)
    GameObj.inv.find { |obj| matches?(obj, name) }
  end

  # a fresh LOOK IN so the IDs are live (cached contents go stale)
  def self.look_in(container)
    fput "look in ##{container.id}"
    container.contents.to_a
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- eloot's keep list
  def self.sell_exclude
    return @sell_exclude if defined?(@sell_exclude)

    path = File.join(DATA_DIR, XMLData.game, Char.name, 'eloot.yaml')
    settings = (YAML.respond_to?(:unsafe_load_file) ? YAML.unsafe_load_file(path) : YAML.load_file(path)) rescue nil
    list = settings.is_a?(Hash) ? Array(settings[:sell_exclude] || settings['sell_exclude']) : []
    @sell_exclude = list.empty? ? nil : Regexp.union(list.map { |entry| /\b(?:#{entry})\b/ })
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- reading the game
  # put, not fput (fput swallows the first reply line). Reads until `done`, or, once a line
  # matching `settle` has been seen, until a second goes by with nothing new.
  def self.collect(action, done, timeout: 6, settle: nil)
    lines = []
    Script.current.clear
    put action
    end_time = Time.now + timeout
    last_line = Time.now
    loop do
      line = get?
      if line
        lines << line
        last_line = Time.now
        if line =~ /^(?:\.\.\.w|W)ait ([0-9]+) sec/
          sleep [Regexp.last_match(1).to_i - 0.5, 0.3].max
          put action
          end_time = Time.now + timeout
          next
        end
        break if line =~ done
      else
        break if settle && Time.now - last_line > 1.0 && lines.any? { |l| l =~ settle }
        sleep 0.1
      end
      break if Time.now > end_time
    end
    lines
  end

  def self.wait_for(seconds)
    end_time = Time.now + seconds
    until yield
      return false if Time.now > end_time
      sleep 0.5
    end
    true
  end

  def self.worst_wound
    Wounds.all_wounds.values.map(&:to_i).max.to_i
  rescue StandardError
    0
  end

  def self.gem_in_hand
    hand = GameObj.right_hand
    hand.id.nil? ? nil : hand
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- moving gems
  def self.hold(gem)
    return true if GameObj.right_hand.id.to_s == gem.id.to_s

    waitrt?
    collect("get ##{gem.id}", GET_DONE, timeout: 4)
    wait_for(2) { GameObj.right_hand.id.to_s == gem.id.to_s }
  end

  # whatever's in the right hand goes into `container`; true if the hand ends up empty
  def self.stash(container)
    hand = gem_in_hand
    return true if hand.nil?

    waitrt?
    lines = collect("put ##{hand.id} in ##{container.id}", PUT_DONE, timeout: 4)
    return true if wait_for(2) { GameObj.right_hand.id.nil? }

    msg "Couldn't put #{hand.name} in #{container.name}: #{lines.last}"
    false
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- staying safe
  # true when it's safe and affordable to sing right now. Waits (up to --mana-wait) for
  # mana and hit points to come back; stuns are waited out.
  def self.ready_to_sing?
    cost = Spell[SPELL].mana_cost
    unless wait_for(60) { !stunned? }
      @stop_reason = 'still stunned after a minute'
      return false
    end
    if worst_wound > 1
      @stop_reason = 'wounded (worse than minor)'
      return false
    end
    if checkhealth < @min_health
      msg "Waiting for #{@min_health} hit points before singing (you have #{checkhealth})."
      unless wait_for(@mana_wait) { checkhealth >= @min_health }
        @stop_reason = "hit points stayed under #{@min_health}"
        return false
      end
    end
    if checkmana < cost
      msg "Waiting for #{cost} mana (you have #{checkmana})."
      unless wait_for(@mana_wait) { checkmana >= cost }
        @stop_reason = "mana stayed under #{cost} for #{@mana_wait} seconds"
        return false
      end
    end
    true
  end

  # eherbs after an explosion. Hands must be empty first (eherbs needs them).
  def self.heal!
    return true if worst_wound <= 1 && checkhealth >= @min_health
    return false if @heal_runs >= 3

    @heal_runs += 1
    msg 'Healing up with eherbs before the next gem.'
    Script.run('eherbs')
    wait_for(5) { worst_wound <= 1 }
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- the song
  def self.prepare
    return true if checkprep == NAME

    waitrt?
    waitcastrt?
    collect('release', /^You feel the magic|^You don't have a prepared spell|^You release|^You let/, timeout: 3) unless checkprep == 'None'
    lines = collect("prepare #{SPELL}", PREP_DONE, timeout: 4)
    return true if wait_for(2) { checkprep == NAME }

    msg "Couldn't prepare #{NAME}. The game said:"
    lines.last(4).each { |line| respond "    #{line}" }
    false
  end

  def self.classify(lines)
    text = lines.join("\n")
    return :shatter  if text =~ SHATTER
    return :orb      if text =~ ESSENCE || text =~ ORB_MAX
    return :max      if text =~ MAX
    return :severe   if text =~ SEVERE
    return :strain   if text =~ STRAIN
    return :somewhat if text =~ SOMEWHAT
    return :misfire  if text =~ MISFIRE
    return :better   if text =~ BETTER
    return :hindered if text =~ HINDERED
    return :not_held if text =~ NOT_HELD
    return :no_mana  if text =~ NO_MANA

    :unknown
  end

  # one song at the gem in the right hand; returns [outcome, lines]
  def self.sing(gem)
    Spell.lock_cast
    begin
      return [:no_prep, []] unless prepare

      # re-read mana right before the SING: never cast short of the full cost
      cost = Spell[SPELL].mana_cost
      return [:no_mana, []] if checkmana < cost

      waitrt?
      waitcastrt?
      lines = collect("sing ##{gem.id}", SING_DONE, timeout: 8, settle: ANSWERED)
      outcome = classify(lines)
      # the hand is the real test of an explosion: no gem, no gem
      outcome = :shatter if outcome != :not_held && gem_in_hand.nil?
      [outcome, lines]
    ensure
      Spell.unlock_cast
    end
  end

  def self.appraise(gem)
    return nil unless @appraise && gem

    waitrt?
    lines = collect("appraise ##{gem.id}", APPRAISE, timeout: 4)
    found = lines.join(' ')[APPRAISE, :value]
    found && found.delete(',').to_i
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- one gem
  def self.finish(gem_name, home, result, rounds)
    dest = result == :orb ? @orbs : (@sung || home)
    hand = gem_in_hand
    unless stash(dest)
      # the orb container is full or gone: back where it came from (eloot will sell it,
      # so say so loudly)
      dest = [home, @sung].compact.find { |container| stash(container) }
      if result == :orb
        @orbs_found.delete(gem_name)
        @orbs_stranded << gem_name
        bold "#{gem_name} is an ORB but wouldn't go in #{@orbs.name}; it's in #{dest ? dest.name : 'your hand'}."
      end
    end
    $fizzpure_done[hand.id.to_s] = result if hand && result != :stopped
    @report << [gem_name, result, rounds]
    msg "#{gem_name}: #{describe(result)} after #{rounds} #{rounds == 1 ? 'song' : 'songs'}#{result == :orb && dest == @orbs ? " -> #{@orbs.name}" : ''}." unless opts[:silent]
  end

  def self.describe(result)
    {
      orb: 'ORB', max: 'as pure as it gets', somewhat: 'stopped at "improves somewhat"',
      strain: 'stopped at "crack loudly and strain"', severe: 'stopped at "severely affecting"',
      misfire: 'song misfired', capped: 'hit --max-rounds', unknown: 'unrecognized reply, stopped',
      hindered: 'armor kept spoiling the song', not_held: 'lost track of it', stopped: 'run stopped'
    }.fetch(result, result.to_s)
  end

  # returns false when the whole run should stop
  def self.purify(gem, home)
    unless hold(gem)
      msg "Couldn't pick up #{gem.name}; skipping it."
      return true
    end
    name = gem.name

    start_value = appraise(gem)
    if @min_value && start_value && start_value < @min_value
      msg "#{name} appraises at #{start_value}, under --min-value; leaving it."
      stash(home)
      return true
    end

    rounds = 0
    hindered = 0
    loop do
      if rounds >= @max_rounds
        finish(name, home, :capped, rounds)
        return true
      end
      unless ready_to_sing?
        finish(name, home, :stopped, rounds)
        return false
      end

      held = gem_in_hand
      if held.nil?
        msg "#{name} isn't in your hand any more; moving on."
        return true
      end
      outcome, lines = sing(held)
      case outcome
      when :better
        rounds += 1
        hindered = 0
      when :hindered
        hindered += 1
        if hindered >= 3
          finish(name, home, :hindered, rounds)
          return true
        end
      when :orb
        rounds += 1
        @orbs_found << name
        track_earnings(start_value)
        finish(name, home, :orb, rounds)
        return true
      when :max, :somewhat, :strain, :severe, :misfire
        rounds += 1
        track_earnings(start_value)
        finish(name, home, outcome, rounds)
        return true
      when :shatter
        @shattered << name
        bold "#{name} exploded after #{rounds + 1} #{rounds.zero? ? 'song' : 'songs'}."
        lines.each { |line| respond "    #{line}" } if lines.none? { |l| l =~ SHATTER }
        @earnings -= start_value if start_value
        return heal! ? true : (@stop_reason = 'still hurt after eherbs'; false)
      when :no_mana, :no_prep
        @stop_reason = outcome == :no_prep ? "couldn't prepare #{NAME}" : 'ran out of mana'
        finish(name, home, :stopped, rounds)
        return false
      else # :not_held, :unknown
        msg "Didn't recognize the reply to singing at #{name}; leaving it. The game said:"
        lines.last(6).each { |line| respond "    #{line}" }
        finish(name, home, outcome, rounds)
        return true
      end
    end
  end

  # the purified gem is still in hand here: appraise it before it's put away
  def self.track_earnings(start_value)
    return unless start_value

    final_value = appraise(gem_in_hand)
    @earnings += final_value - start_value if final_value
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- the run
  def self.candidates(container)
    words = list_opt(:filter)
    look_in(container).select { |obj|
      obj.type.to_s.split(',').include?('gem') &&
        obj.name !~ SKIP_NAMES &&
        !(sell_exclude && obj.name =~ sell_exclude) &&
        !$fizzpure_done.key?(obj.id.to_s) &&
        (words.empty? || words.any? { |word| obj.name.include?(word) })
    }
  end

  def self.setup
    $fizzpure_done ||= {}
    @report     = []
    @orbs_found = []
    @orbs_stranded = []
    @shattered  = []
    @earnings   = 0
    @heal_runs  = 0
    @max_rounds = int_opt(:max_rounds, 20)
    @min_health = int_opt(:min_health, 70)
    @mana_wait  = int_opt(:mana_wait, 600)
    @appraise   = Skills.trading > 24
    @min_value  = opts[:min_value] ? opts[:min_value].to_i : nil
    msg '--min-value needs 25 ranks of Trading to APPRAISE; ignoring it.' if @min_value && !@appraise
    @min_value = nil unless @appraise

    unless Spell[SPELL].known?
      msg "You don't know #{NAME} (#{SPELL})."
      exit
    end

    raw_names = list_opt(:raw)
    if raw_names.empty? || opts[:orbs].nil? || opts[:help]
      respond <<~HELP
        [fizzpure #{VERSION}] purify gems with #{NAME} (#{SPELL})
          ;fizzpure --raw=cloak --orbs=linen.pouch
          ;fizzpure --raw=cloak,backpack,haversack --orbs=linen.pouch --dry-run
          --raw= (required) --orbs= (required) --sung= --filter= --max-rounds=20
          --min-value= --min-health=70 --mana-wait=600 --dry-run --silent
      HELP
      exit
    end

    @raw = raw_names.map { |name|
      found = find_container(name)
      msg "Can't find a container called #{name}; skipping it." unless found
      found
    }.compact
    @orbs = find_container(opts[:orbs])
    @sung = opts[:sung] && find_container(opts[:sung])
    unless @orbs
      msg "Can't find your orb container (#{opts[:orbs]}). Not singing: an orb would get sold."
      exit
    end
    if opts[:sung] && @sung.nil?
      msg "Can't find --sung=#{opts[:sung]}."
      exit
    end
    if @raw.any? { |container| container.id == @orbs.id }
      msg "The orb container is also one of the --raw containers; pick a separate one."
      exit
    end
  end

  def self.main
    setup
    work = @raw.flat_map { |container| candidates(container).map { |gem| [gem, container] } }
    if work.empty?
      msg 'No gems to purify.'
      return
    end

    if opts[:dry_run]
      msg "Would sing to #{work.size} #{work.size == 1 ? 'gem' : 'gems'}:"
      work.each { |gem, home|
        note = gem.name =~ TINY_PEARL ? " (tiny pearl: straight to #{@orbs.name})" : ''
        respond "    #{gem.name} in #{home.name}#{note}"
      }
      return
    end

    before_dying { FizzPure.cleanup }
    empty_hands
    @emptied_hands = true
    unless heal!
      msg "Too hurt to sing safely (#{@stop_reason || 'wounds'}); leaving the gems."
      return
    end

    work.each_with_index { |(gem, home), index|
      if gem.name =~ TINY_PEARL
        @current_home = home
        if hold(gem)
          @orbs_found << gem.name
          finish(gem.name, home, :orb, 0)
        end
        next
      end
      @current_home = home
      next if purify(gem, home)

      left = work.size - index
      bold "Stopping: #{@stop_reason}. #{left} #{left == 1 ? 'gem' : 'gems'} left as #{left == 1 ? 'it is' : 'they are'}."
      break
    }
    @current_home = nil
    summary
  end

  def self.summary
    sung = @report.count { |_, result, _| ![:stopped, :not_held, :unknown].include?(result) }
    text = "Done: #{sung} #{sung == 1 ? 'gem' : 'gems'} sung"
    text << ", #{@orbs_found.size} #{@orbs_found.size == 1 ? 'orb' : 'orbs'} -> #{@orbs.name} (#{@orbs_found.join(', ')})" unless @orbs_found.empty?
    text << ", #{@shattered.size} exploded (#{@shattered.join(', ')})" unless @shattered.empty?
    text << ", #{@orbs_stranded.size} ORB(S) LEFT WHERE ELOOT WILL SELL THEM (#{@orbs_stranded.join(', ')})" unless @orbs_stranded.empty?
    text << ", worth #{@earnings >= 0 ? '+' : ''}#{@earnings} silver" if @appraise
    bold "#{text}."
  end

  # ;kill or a crash: put a gem in hand back where it came from
  def self.cleanup
    Spell.unlock_cast
    if gem_in_hand && @current_home && GameObj.right_hand.type.to_s.split(',').include?('gem')
      stash(@sung || @current_home)
    end
    fill_hands if @emptied_hands
  rescue StandardError => e
    respond "[fizzpure] cleanup: #{e.message}"
  end
end

FizzPure.main
